# Web3 Authentication

Lux can authenticate wallets with Sign-In with Ethereum (EIP-4361), verify
personal-sign signatures, issue expiring sessions, evaluate role permissions,
check token-gated access, and validate multi-signature thresholds.

The framework covers:

- EIP-4361 message generation, parsing, validation, and authentication
- Ethereum personal-sign signature recovery
- multi-signature threshold checks
- role and permission management
- session expiry, refresh, revocation, and audit events
- ERC-20/ERC-721-style token gates over normalized holdings

## Sign-In with Ethereum

```elixir
alias Lux.Web3.Auth
alias Lux.Web3.Auth.SIWE

message =
  SIWE.build_message(%{
    domain: "app.lux.dev",
    address: "0x7E5F4552091A69125d5DfCb7b8C2659029395Bdf",
    statement: "Sign in to Lux",
    uri: "https://app.lux.dev",
    chain_id: 1,
    nonce: "abc12345",
    issued_at: DateTime.utc_now() |> DateTime.to_iso8601()
  })

{:ok, %{siwe: siwe, session: session}} =
  Auth.sign_in(message, "0x...", domain: "app.lux.dev", chain_id: 1, roles: [:member])
```

## Authorization

```elixir
alias Lux.Web3.Auth
alias Lux.Web3.Auth.RBAC

policy =
  RBAC.new()
  |> RBAC.put_role(:member, [%{action: :read, resource: :workspace}])

:ok = Auth.authorize_session(session, policy, :read, :workspace)
```

## Token Gates

```elixir
alias Lux.Web3.Auth.TokenGate

holdings = %{{1, "0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000abc"} => 10}

TokenGate.allowed?(holdings, [
  %{chain_id: 1, contract: "0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000abc", min_balance: 1}
])
```

## Multi-Signature Thresholds

```elixir
alias Lux.Web3.Auth.MultiSig

MultiSig.verify_threshold(message, signatures, owners, 2)
```
